Fixed in 7b786c5. The empty-turn fallback no longer shadows recipe retry — it now runs *inside* the `None => handle_retry_logic(...)` arm. `handle_retry_logic` returns the granular `RetryResult` again (instead of a collapsed `bool`), so the arm distinguishes:

- `Retried` → restart the loop (recipe retry took over);
- `Skipped` (no `retry_config`) **and** `empty_response` → the bounded empty-turn retry/fallback;
- everything else (`SuccessChecksPassed`, `MaxAttemptsReached`, or a non-empty turn) → exit as before.

So a recipe with `retry_config` always gets its success checks / `on_failure` / `max_retries` first; the generic empty-response message only appears when no recipe retry is configured. Added `test_empty_turn_defers_to_recipe_retry` (empty provider turn + passing-check recipe must not surface the fallback); verified it fails against the old shadowing order.

This was the fifth instance of the same shadowing class (last-assistant-text, persist-before-clear, steer, final-output, and now recipe retry), and restructuring in 30b2ef1 to route through the completion `match` is what made this one a two-line ordering change rather than another special-case guard.

